{title: What A Friend We Have In Jesus}
{key: Bb}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Bb]What a friend we have in Je[Eb]sus,
[Bb]All our sins and griefs to [F]bear!
[Bb]What a privilege to car[Eb]ry
[Bb]Every-[F]thing to God in [Bb]prayer
[Cm]Oh, what peace we often for[Bb]feit,
[Eb]Oh, what need[Bb]less pain we [F]bear
[Bb]All because we do not car[Eb]ry
[Bb]Everyt[F]hing to God in pray[Bb]er.

{comment: Verse 2}
[Bb]Have we trials and tempta[Eb]tions?
[Bb]Is there trouble any[F]where?
[Bb]We should never be discou[Eb]raged,
[Bb]Take it [F]to the Lord in [Bb]prayer.
[Cm]Can we find a friend so [Bb]faithful?
[Eb]Who will [Bb]all our sorrows [F]share?
[Bb]Jesus knows our every weak[Eb]ness,
[Bb]Take it [F]to the Lord in [Bb]prayer.

{comment: Verse 3}
[Bb]Are we weak and heavy la[Eb]den,
Cum[Bb]bered with a load of [F]care?
[Bb]Precious Savior, still our re[Eb]fuge
[Bb]Take it [F]to the Lord in [Bb]prayer.
